-       Div(P("Hello"))
+       Div(P("Hello"))

=       Div(P("Hello"))
-       ```
+       ```

-       `Whatwg` is the HTML Living Standard, what "HTML" means today, and suits almost every
-       use; `Html4Transitional` is HTML 4.01 Transitional, for a program which must emit or
-       read that dialect's presentational tags and attributes. Reading (`read[Html]`,
-       `load[Html]`) needs a `Dom` in scope; rendering with `show` always uses the WHATWG one,
-       and a streamed `Document[Html]` uses the DOM recorded in its `Html.Provenance`.
+       `Whatwg` es el HTML Living Standard, lo que hoy significa «HTML», y sirve para casi
+       cualquier uso; `Html4Transitional` es HTML 4.01 Transitional, para un programa que deba
+       emitir o leer las etiquetas y los atributos de presentación de ese dialecto. La lectura
+       (`read[Html]`, `load[Html]`) necesita un `Dom` en el ámbito; la representación con
+       `show` usa siempre el de WHATWG, y un `Document[Html]` emitido como flujo usa el DOM
+       registrado en su `Html.Provenance`.

=       and a streamed `Document[Html]` uses the DOM recorded in its `Html.Provenance`.
-   refer honeycomb.Whatwg
+   refer honeycomb.Whatwg

=       and a streamed `Document[Html]` uses the DOM recorded in its `Html.Provenance`.
=   refer honeycomb.Whatwg
