- entry .attributives   `Attributive` givens which widen what an attribute accepts, to import by name
+ entry .attributives   givens `Attributive` que amplían lo que acepta un atributo, para importar por nombre

= entry .attributives   `Attributive` givens which widen what an attribute accepts, to import by name
-   detail
+   detail

-       An attribute's value is typed: `width` takes a positive integer, `src` a URL, `disabled`
-       a presence, so `Img(width = 64)` compiles and `Img(width = 1.5)` does not. The
-       `Attributive` instances in `Attributive`'s companion cover the common types; where an
-       attribute type has no instance for the value in hand, `textAttributive` makes a `Text`
-       acceptable for every attribute, so `Img(src = t"image.jpg")` stands where a URL is
-       expected. It is imported by name, since it deliberately bypasses the attribute's type.
+       El valor de un atributo tiene tipo: `width` admite un entero positivo, `src` una URL,
+       `disabled` una presencia, de modo que `Img(width = 64)` compila y `Img(width = 1.5)` no.
+       Las instancias de `Attributive` del objeto compañero de `Attributive` cubren los tipos
+       habituales; cuando el tipo de un atributo no tiene instancia para el valor del que se
+       dispone, `textAttributive` hace que un `Text` sea aceptable para cualquier atributo, de
+       modo que `Img(src = t"image.jpg")` vale donde se espera una URL. Se importa por nombre,
+       porque se salta deliberadamente el tipo del atributo.

=       expected. It is imported by name, since it deliberately bypasses the attribute's type.
-   refer honeycomb.Attributive
+   refer honeycomb.Attributive

-   entry .textAttributive   a `Text` is acceptable as the value of any attribute, written as it is
-       `[target] => Text is Attributive to target`: the text becomes the attribute's value
-       unchanged, whatever the attribute's declared type. With it in scope, `src = t"x.jpg"`,
-       `width = t"64"` and `onclick = t"…"` all compile; without it, each needs a value of the
-       attribute's own type.
+   entry .textAttributive   un `Text` es aceptable como valor de cualquier atributo, escrito tal cual
+       `[target] => Text is Attributive to target`: el texto se convierte en el valor del
+       atributo sin cambios, sea cual sea el tipo declarado del atributo. Con él en el ámbito,
+       `src = t"x.jpg"`, `width = t"64"` y `onclick = t"…"` compilan todos; sin él, cada uno
+       necesita un valor del tipo propio del atributo.

