- entry .Tag   an HTML tag as a value: applied to attributes and children, it makes an element
+ entry .Tag   una etiqueta HTML como valor: aplicada a atributos e hijos, construye un elemento

= entry .Tag   an HTML tag as a value: applied to attributes and children, it makes an element
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `Tag` is the builder for one element name, and every `val` of a `Dom` such as
-       `Whatwg` — `Div`, `P`, `Img`, `Table` — is one. It is itself an `Html.Element` (the
-       empty element of its name, which is why `Br` alone is `<br>` and `Title` alone
-       `<title></title>`), and applying it makes a new element: named arguments are
-       attributes, positional arguments are children, and attributes come first.
+       Un `Tag` es el constructor de un nombre de elemento, y cada `val` de un `Dom` como `Whatwg`
+       (`Div`, `P`, `Img`, `Table`) es uno. Es a su vez un `Html.Element` (el elemento vacío de su
+       nombre, y por eso `Br` solo es `<br>` y `Title` solo `<title></title>`), y al aplicarlo se
+       construye un elemento nuevo: los argumentos con nombre son atributos, los argumentos
+       posicionales son hijos, y los atributos van primero.

=       attributes, positional arguments are children, and attributes come first.
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       attributes, positional arguments are children, and attributes come first.
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

